error[E0277]: `UInt<u8, 3>` has no atomic bitwise operations
 --> tests/compile_fail/arbitrary_int/bitwise_on_an_arbitrary_width_integer.rs:9:29
  |
9 |     Atomic::new(u3::new(0)).not(Relaxed);
  |                             ^^^ `and`, `or`, `xor`, `not`, their `fetch_` forms, and `bit_set`, `bit_clear` and `bit_toggle` need `AtomBitwise`
  |
  = help: the trait `AtomBitwise` is not implemented for `UInt<u8, 3>`
  = note: for your own newtype over a value that has it, derive it: `#[derive(AtomBitwise)]`
  = note: for a pointer, whose bits are its address, keep tags beside it in a derived pointer word, whose tag fields have `or`, `and` and `xor`
  = note: to change the value in a compare-exchange loop, call `update`
  = help: the following other types implement trait `AtomBitwise`:
            Saturating<T>
            Wrapping<T>
            bool
            i16
            i32
            i64
            i8
            isize
          and $N others
